Day 4: Windows Virtual Machine Setup

Project Overview
This lab focused on expanding the cybersecurity home lab by creating a Windows virtual machine within VirtualBox. The objective was to understand how multiple operating systems can operate within a virtualized environment and establish a target machine for future cybersecurity activities.

Environment

Host Operating System	Windows
Virtualization Software	VirtualBox
Guest Operating Systems	Kali Linux, Windows
Network Type	Virtual Lab Environment

Objectives

Create a Windows virtual machine
Configure virtual machine resources
Explore basic Windows administration tools
Understand user accounts and permissions
Identify network configuration information
Prepare a target system for future security testing

Tasks Completed

Created a Windows virtual machine using VirtualBox
Allocated memory, storage, and processor resources
Installed and configured Windows
Explored Windows Settings and Control Panel
Reviewed Task Manager and running processes
Examined Windows Security settings
Located system network information using Command Prompt
Explored Event Viewer and available log categories

Key Concepts Learned

Virtual Machines
Virtual machines allow multiple operating systems to run on a single physical computer. This provides an isolated environment for testing, learning, and security research without affecting the host operating system.

User Accounts
Windows uses user accounts to control access to system resources. Understanding account permissions is an important part of cybersecurity because access management plays a significant role in protecting systems from unauthorized activity.

Event Logging
Windows records system activity through logs. These logs can be used to investigate system events, security incidents, application activity, and user actions.

Network Configuration
Each machine connected to a network requires its own network configuration information. Understanding device communication is essential before performing network analysis and scanning activities.

